								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg1673#msg1673"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg1673#msg1673">Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #18 on:</b> September 17, 2003, 10:14:15 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Kinladar link=board=1;threadid=320;start=15#msg1664 date=1063718233</div><div class="quote">. This is of course my personal opinion, and feel free to tell me I'm full of it &nbsp;;D<br /><br />RoS deserves more credit because they've been able to accomplish far more than anyone probably thought they could. They zipped through alot of content pretty quick in PoP once they focused on it. Now that they have gained alot of nice upgrades in PoP, them getting VT access is simply a matter of getting the members all keyed, and downing the Emp. If they can take Rallos Zek, they can take Emp. I just personally consider RoS a more skilled guild is all. Anyone can post thier own revisions though.<br /><br /></div><br />Kin, you are full of it :P &nbsp; hehe couldnt resist.<br /><br />Anyways, I would tend to weight the actuall action over the speed at which it was attained, which is the primary reason for your placement of RoS. Life in EQ is much easier now for any guild. Gear is better and cheaper, there has been incredible implosion of the mid range guilds, resulting in a freeing up of talent, that untill recently (started in the spring of this year) was unavailable. Additionally, there is a bigger pool of 65's to draw from. Encounters are mapped, simplified, and revealed already on sites. Simply put it is easier now than it has been for previous guilds.<br /><br />This is not to sell short what RoS has done. They HAVE progressed at an incredible rate, and do appear to be VERY skilled and focused. My caution is moving them up because of their speed, rather than purely what they have accomplished. If you do that, then you are going to have to go back and look at the difficulty many other guilds had comming up.<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
